\details{
This function implements an indifference zone approach for group selection in
repeated measures designs. It determines:
\itemize{
\item PMD: Probability that any decision is made (i.e., at least one comparison
is statistically significant)
\item PCD: Probability that the correct group is identified as best, given that
a decision is made
}

The indifference zone is defined such that the best group has a mean delta standard
deviations larger than all other groups. The function simulates from this configuration
to estimate PMD and PCD.

The critical p-value is computed using \code{rmanc.best.crit} unless provided.
Decisions are based on the best group selection procedure applied to trimmed means.
